  "proves": [
    "Cross-host signal transport works: process A on one machine publishes, process B on another machine reads the same signal.",
    "Signal ordering within a mission survives the transport (sequence 1 then 2, read back in that order).",
    "Idempotency is persistent, not process-local: an identical re-publish from a third, separate OS process returned duplicate=true at the original sequence.",
    "The seed identity guard read the expected seed id on both hosts before any read or write.",
    "Content fidelity: every field of every signal read on ichabodcrane deep-equals what JustinLenovo published, plus the derived sequence."
  ],
  "doesNotProve": [
    "The doctrine baseline loop (Agent A -> Agent B with zero human intervention) is NOT complete. This is transport only.",
    "Shared mission state across hosts is still missing: packages/mission/src/mission-store.js is local-filesystem only, so the two hosts do not share authoritative mission state.",
    "Remote executor dispatch is still missing: there is no path for a mission on one host to make an executor on another host perform work.",
    "createMissionOrchestrator still defaults to the in-memory bus. Nothing in the orchestrator uses this transport yet; it is opt-in via injection.",
    "The orchestrator publish() path still swallows bus errors and its return value is discarded, so a transport failure would not surface through the orchestrator today. Unchanged in this run and reported as a residual blocker.",
    "No consumer/subscription semantics: read() returns the whole mission stream. There is no blocking read, no consumer group, no at-least-once delivery tracking.",
    "Single seed host. No replication or failover; if ichabodcrane is down the transport is down."
  ]
